    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d410">

                <pb facs="0523" n="429" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg429"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.124a/91: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Liberia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Reber</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-09-19T14:00:00-04:00">September 19, 1930—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>80. Your 119, September 15, 9 p.m. The Department has received copy of Hines’
                    radio received September 17 in Akron, quoting the text of proposed letter from
                    Finance Corporation in answer to Liberian Government request for sanitation
                    funds. Robinson<anchor n="5" xml:id="d410-f1"/> comments “I am a little
                    surprised that he does not suggest the immediate giving to the Sanitary Adviser
                    of governmental authority, sanitary police corps and Sanitary Court by Executive
                    Order to be subsequently <pb facs="0524" n="430" xml:id="pg430"/> confirmed by
                    legislature if that action required to be legally effective there”.</p>
                <p>The Department also notes that Dr. Smith holds similar view as expressed in third
                    paragraph of your September 15, 9 p.m. and it believes that without this
                    authority in addition to direct disbursement of the funds by Dr. Smith the
                    campaign could not be effectively carried on. Please discuss with Loomis and
                    report.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d410-f1" n="5" xml:id="d410-f1-content">
                <p>B. N. Robinson, assistant secretary of the Firestone Tire &amp; Rubber Co. and
                    Attorney of the Firestone Plantations Co., Akron, Ohio.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
